# Claude Code agent worktrees — transient; never commit as gitlinks
.claude/worktrees/

# Supabase CLI scratch state — the ref/version files it rewrites on every
# invocation, including `npm run db:types`. `supabase link` regenerates them and
# the tracked config.toml already carries project_id, which is what gen-types
# reads. This is what `supabase init` puts in .gitignore upstream; it was simply
# never applied here, so `cli-latest` churned a commit every CLI upgrade.
supabase/.temp/

# graphify: 25MB of tool output, none of it authored. Ignored wholesale.
#
# Every file here is regenerated by `/graphify` from the working tree, so a
# checkout of them is worthless to anyone else — and partial tracking is what
# made this a problem. graphify-out/cache/ alone is 1,103 content-addressed AST
# fragments keyed by the SHA-256 of the file each was parsed from, which made
# the editor's SCM badge read "1K+" and buried the pending work that was real.
# The three files that WERE tracked churned as hard: one graph.json refresh is
# a 300,000-line diff against an 8.8MB blob every clone pays for forever.
#
# The consumers already assume it may be absent: scripts/graph-diff.js exits
# with "run graphify first", and the rulebook/docs merely describe the artifact.
# Regenerate with `/graphify`.
graphify-out/

# ECC payloads for non-Claude harnesses (Codex/Antigravity, pi) — not used by Claude Code
.claude/.agents/
.claude/.pi/

# ECC harness (Everything Claude Code, project-scope install) is LOCAL tooling.
# Its hook commands embed this machine's home path, so it cannot run elsewhere,
# and it is ~550 third-party files. These patterns only hide UNTRACKED files:
# the team's own agents (planner, code-reviewer, compliance-specialist, ...),
# agent-memory, mcp.json and settings*.json stay versioned. Add a new
# project-owned agent or skill with `git add -f`.
# ECC's edits to the tracked .claude/settings.json are hidden locally with
# `git update-index --skip-worktree .claude/settings.json`
# (undo with --no-skip-worktree before changing that file on purpose).
.claude/AGENTS.md
.claude/PLUGIN_SCHEMA_NOTES.md
.claude/README.md
.claude/the-security-guide.md
.claude/marketplace.json
.claude/plugin.json
.claude/agents/
.claude/commands/
.claude/ecc/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/mcp-configs/
.claude/rules/
.claude/scripts/
.claude/skills/

# Local scratch and one-off artifacts. scratch/ holds personal data
